[TITLE]
L-Town: two-source parallel second-order (2R/2RA) chlorine reactions, EXBRUF wall reaction, THM and HAA (after Kastl et al. 1999; Fisher et al. 2011, 2012, 2015, 2017, 2023)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Parallel second-order ("two-reactant", 2R) chlorine model in EPANET-MSX form.
; Written for the epanet-msx-review benchmarks as a stand-in for InfoWater MSX's
; built-in "PSM" examples, whose formulation is not public. Equations follow the
; open literature; this file is our own implementation, not a copy of any listing.
;
; Bulk reactions (Kastl, Fisher & Jegatheesan 1999, J. Water SRT-Aqua 48(6):219,
; doi:10.2166/aqua.1999.0024; Fisher, Kastl & Sathasivan 2011, Water Res.
; 45:4896, doi:10.1016/j.watres.2011.06.032):
;   dF/dt  = -kF * F * Cl          fast reducing agents  [mg Cl-equiv/L]
;   dS/dt  = -kS * S * Cl          slow reducing agents  [mg Cl-equiv/L]
;   dCl/dt =  dF/dt + dS/dt (+ wall term in pipes)
; Rate coefficients carry the Arrhenius factor of the 2RA model (Fisher, Kastl &
; Sathasivan 2012, Water Res. 46:3293, doi:10.1016/j.watres.2012.03.017):
;   k(TC) = k20 * exp(EOR*(TC-20)/(293*(TC+273)))
; Here TC is a fixed water temperature (default 20 C, so the factor is 1);
; ltown-temperature.msx makes the temperature a dynamic species.
;
; Two source waters. Each reservoir carries its own reactant pair, and each
; pair keeps its own rate coefficients when the waters blend; all four react
; with the one chlorine pool (the blending approach of Fisher et al. 2015,
; J. Environ. Eng. 141, doi:10.1061/(ASCE)EE.1943-7870.0000980, as described
; in Fisher 2023, Water Environ. Res. 95:e10949, doi:10.1002/wer.10949).
;   Water A (R1): Greenvale, Australia. 2RA coefficients and reactant
;     concentrations from I. Fisher, "A Multi-Species Decay Model to Support
;     Cost-Effective Chlorination in Distribution Systems", Bentley Virtuosity
;     blog, 24 Mar 2022 (data of Fisher et al. 2011, 2012).
;   Water B (R2): Mirrabooka, Western Australia. Coefficients and reactant
;     concentrations of Fisher 2023 (WER) Table 4.
;
; Wall reaction EXBRUF (Fisher, Kastl & Sathasivan 2017, Water Res. 125:427,
; doi:10.1016/j.watres.2017.08.066; 2023, Urban Water J. 20:1157,
; doi:10.1080/1573062X.2023.2241437; MSX form in Fisher 2023 WER Tables 5-6):
;   RW  = -BA*Cl/(1 + BA/KM)           [mg/dm2/h]
;   BA  = ABF20*TCOEFW*exp(-BBF*Cl)    biofilm activity [dm/h]
;   KM  = SH*DCL/D                     mass-transfer coefficient [dm/h]
;   SH  = Gnielinski, rough pipe:  (f/8)(Re-1000)Sc / (1 + 12.7 (f/8)^0.5 (Sc^0.66 - 1))
;   pipe rate adds (4/D)*RW, D in dm.
; Deviations from Fisher's listing (see models/literature.md):
;   * f from Swamee-Jain with a fixed roughness, not MSX's Ff, which is NaN at
;     zero flow; the log is squared by multiplication, because MSX returns 0 for
;     x^y when x <= 0;
;   * Gnielinski is used only for Re > 2300; below that, EPANET's laminar
;     Sherwood number (Graetz form) is used, as Gnielinski is not defined there;
;   * the Re given to Gnielinski is clamped to >= 2300 so that the unused branch
;     stays finite;
;   * Sc^0.66 is its own term: this MSX version reads ")-1" as ") -1" (a
;     negative number) and rejects the expression.
; By-products (Fisher 2023 WER Table 4, after Sathasivan et al. 2020 and
; Premarathna et al. 2022): dTHM/dt = -KTHM*dCl/dt, dHAA/dt = -KHAA*dCl/dt,
; with dCl/dt the total chlorine reaction rate, as in Fisher's listing.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

[OPTIONS]
  AREA_UNITS  M2             ;not used (no wall species); as in Fisher's listing
  RATE_UNITS  HR             ;rates in concentration per hour
  SOLVER      RK5            ;as in Fisher 2023 WER Table 4
  COUPLING    NONE           ;no equilibrium equations
  TIMESTEP    300            ;s
  RTOL        0.001          ;as in Fisher 2023 WER Table 4
  ATOL        0.0001         ;as in Fisher 2023 WER Table 4

[SPECIES]
  BULK  CL    MG             ;free chlorine [mg/L]
  BULK  FA    MG             ;fast reducing agents of water A (R1) [mg Cl-equiv/L]
  BULK  SA    MG             ;slow reducing agents of water A (R1) [mg Cl-equiv/L]
  BULK  FB    MG             ;fast reducing agents of water B (R2) [mg Cl-equiv/L]
  BULK  SB    MG             ;slow reducing agents of water B (R2) [mg Cl-equiv/L]
  BULK  THM   MG             ;total trihalomethanes [mg/L]
  BULK  HAA   MG             ;haloacetic acids [mg/L]

[COEFFICIENTS]
  CONSTANT  LU  1.0     ;metres per network length unit: 1 for SI networks, 0.3048 for US units
; water temperature for this run [C]
  CONSTANT  TC     20.0
; water A (R1), Greenvale: 2RA coefficients at 20 C
  CONSTANT  KFA20  0.164      ;fast rate coefficient [L/mg/h]
  CONSTANT  KSA20  0.00496    ;slow rate coefficient [L/mg/h]
  CONSTANT  EORA   10500      ;activation energy / gas constant [K]
; water B (R2), Mirrabooka: 2RA coefficients at 20 C
  CONSTANT  KFB20  0.0054     ;fast rate coefficient [L/mg/h]
  CONSTANT  KSB20  0.0017     ;slow rate coefficient [L/mg/h]
  CONSTANT  EORB   1300       ;activation energy / gas constant [K]
; by-product yields (Fisher 2023 WER defaults)
  CONSTANT  KTHM   0.043      ;[mg THM / mg Cl reacted]
  CONSTANT  KHAA   0.020      ;[mg HAA / mg Cl reacted]
; EXBRUF wall reaction (Fisher 2023 WER Tables 5-6, Mirrabooka pipeline)
  CONSTANT  ABF20  1000       ;biofilm activity at zero chlorine and 20 C [dm/h]
  CONSTANT  BBF    26         ;decrease of biofilm activity with chlorine [L/mg]
  CONSTANT  EORW   5000       ;wall E/R [K] ("typical" value in Fisher 2023 WER)
  CONSTANT  EPS    0.0025     ;absolute pipe roughness [m] (Fisher 2023 WER Table 6)

[TERMS]
  ;lengths and velocities in metres: LU is metres per network length unit
  DLU     D*LU
  LLU     Len*LU
; Arrhenius factors relative to 20 C (2RA model)
  TCA     exp(EORA*(TC-20)/(20+273)/(TC+273))
  TCB     exp(EORB*(TC-20)/(20+273)/(TC+273))
  TCW     exp(EORW*(TC-20)/(20+273)/(TC+273))
; bulk reactions of each water's reactants with the common chlorine pool [mg/L/h]
  RFA     -KFA20*TCA*CL*FA
  RSA     -KSA20*TCA*CL*SA
  RFB     -KFB20*TCB*CL*FB
  RSB     -KSB20*TCB*CL*SB
  RB      RFA + RSA + RFB + RSB
; water properties at TC (Fisher 2023 WER eqs 11-12)
  KV      exp(-3.7188 + 578.92/(TC + 135.56))*1E-6   ;kinematic viscosity [m2/s]
  DCL     (0.0365*TC + 0.5176)*1E-9                   ;chlorine diffusivity [m2/s]
  SC      KV/DCL                                      ;Schmidt number
; Sherwood number. Turbulent: Gnielinski with Swamee-Jain friction factor
  RET     Re + STEP(2300 - Re)*(2300 - Re)            ;Re, but at least 2300
  LGF     LOG10(0.27*EPS/DLU + 5.74/(RET^0.9))
  FD8     0.25/(LGF*LGF)/8                            ;Darcy friction factor / 8
  SC66    SC^0.66
  SHT     FD8*(RET - 1000)*SC/(1 + 12.7*(FD8^0.5)*(SC66 - 1))
; laminar: EPANET's developing-flow form
  GZ      DLU*Re*SC/LLU
  SHL     3.65 + 0.0668*GZ/(1 + 0.04*(GZ^0.6667))
  SH      SHL + STEP(Re - 2300)*(SHT - SHL)
  KM      SH*DCL*10/DLU*3600                            ;mass-transfer coefficient [dm/h]
; EXBRUF wall reaction
  BA      ABF20*TCW*exp(-BBF*CL)                      ;biofilm activity [dm/h]
  RW      -BA*CL/(1 + BA/KM)                          ;wall reaction [mg/dm2/h]
  RP      RB + 4/(DLU*10)*RW                            ;total chlorine rate in a pipe [mg/L/h]

[PIPES]
  RATE  CL   RP
  RATE  FA   RFA
  RATE  SA   RSA
  RATE  FB   RFB
  RATE  SB   RSB
  RATE  THM  -KTHM*RP
  RATE  HAA  -KHAA*RP

[TANKS]
; bulk reactions only
  RATE  CL   RB
  RATE  FA   RFA
  RATE  SA   RSA
  RATE  FB   RFB
  RATE  SB   RSB
  RATE  THM  -KTHM*RB
  RATE  HAA  -KHAA*RB

[QUALITY]
; Initial network water: 50/50 blend of waters A and B after 6 h of bulk
; reaction at 20 C from the source state below (computed offline; see models/literature.md).
  GLOBAL  CL   0.473
  GLOBAL  FA   0.301
  GLOBAL  SA   1.408
  GLOBAL  FB   2.002
  GLOBAL  SB   24.76
  GLOBAL  THM  0.0227
  GLOBAL  HAA  0.0105
; R1: water A (Greenvale) dosed to 1.0 mg/L
  NODE  R1  CL   1.0
  NODE  R1  FA   1.13
  NODE  R1  SA   2.87
  NODE  R1  FB   0.0
  NODE  R1  SB   0.0
  NODE  R1  THM  0.0
  NODE  R1  HAA  0.0
; R2: water B (Mirrabooka) dosed to 1.0 mg/L
  NODE  R2  CL   1.0
  NODE  R2  FA   0.0
  NODE  R2  SA   0.0
  NODE  R2  FB   4.1
  NODE  R2  SB   49.9
  NODE  R2  THM  0.0
  NODE  R2  HAA  0.0

[REPORT]
; near R1 (n303) and R2 (n336); blended water at the pump inlet (n54); the tank;
; far from the sources (n215 about 9 h from R1, n187 about 17 h from R2);
; n1, still mostly initial water after 24 h
  NODES    n303 n336 n54 T1 n215 n187 n1
  SPECIES  CL   YES  3
  SPECIES  THM  YES  4
